e same cut. When the edges of positive capacity do not connect the graph, the cut","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of value zero whose source side is the first vertex’s component, with every crossing edge","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(all of capacity zero). Parallel capacities add; self-loops are ignored. ","type":"text"},{"code":"capacity","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"called once per non-loop edge, in position order, before any work (self-loops are never","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"asked). O(nm log n) in the worst case, far less when contractions are many.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/flows\/graphprotocols\/graph\/minimumcut(capacity:)"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/Graph":{"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Graph","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Graph","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/graph","type":"topic","role":"symbol","title":"Graph","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An undirected graph: a finite set of vertices and a finite collection of undirected edges"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"between them. Kept apart from "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DirectedGraph"},{"type":"text","text":": an undirected graph is not a symmetric directed"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"one, and no type is both. ","type":"text"},{"code":"directed","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" views it as one when an algorithm needs arcs.","type":"text"}]},"doc://Flows/documentation/Flows/GraphProtocols/Graph/edmondsKarpMaximumFlow(from:to:capacity:)":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"edmondsKarpMaximumFlow"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","te